{"timestamp": 1778557525.480354, "duration_sec": 2.7747814655303955, "validator_hotkey": "5HNe4Yx7idMcgrsoPogLVko2AA8Pap33aNyXQhpwBxsS4H4Q", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Usually for me, it's actually the evening. Because realistically, I have kids now. I have dinner events or just evening events almost every night. And so really the pause and the silence in my day is after 9.30 at night when I can sit down for a few hours and think about"], [0, "Yeah, that's great. I think we have a tendency in our culture to feel like to get anything done, we have to constantly be on and constantly be moving. And like you're saying, responding to that inundation, trying to stay afloat. But what you're saying sounds a lot like kind of meditative in a way, not necessarily like"], [0, "true meditation, but having some time to contemplate and really look at the things that you're trying to do more from a backed up perspective, like a zoomed out perspective. Yeah. I mean, we'll say it again. I mean,"], [0, "I was just saying that it's so what you're saying sounds like it sounds a lot like a meditative approach to to work. So, sure, we have a lot of, you know, minute things that we have to respond to. Like, you can't just turn off your email inbox and express it."], [0, "expect your co-workers to appreciate it but uh but there's also a time for us to kind of zoom back or zoom out rather and and look at our work from you know the the long perspective got it yeah no i mean certainly you know and a lot of this is discipline you know i think that a lot of the"], [0, "Maybe one of the skills of the 21st century will be the ability to disconnect and to have some discipline over the way that tech drives 