suasive in my particular case, but sometimes you can plant a seed. And I think that's what happened here. A few seeds were planted in my head that now when I see these particular expressions, I go like, you know what?"], [0, "A, that could have been me. On either side, I could have been the one dunking or I could be the one dunking on. Neither of them feel great. We should have a little bit of grace. We should give it five minutes. We should realize that we would have liked someone to reach out to us and say like, hey, do you know about this? And then we can have a fair game discussion. And it doesn't mean kumbaya. It doesn't mean no tension. It doesn't mean that we will all agree about everything if we just talk about it. I also find that to be other bullshit."], [0, "But you know what? There's an opportunity that we would. There's totally an opportunity that, you know, you have that conversation. You're like, oh, yeah, I didn't see that. Yeah. Sorry. My bad. Let me just fix it. Rather than let's light Vesuvio on fire. So question for you guys as co-founders and business partners. Do you guys ever see what the other person has put out social media or otherwise and been like, hey, you maybe shouldn't have said that?"], [0, "Do you guys have that kind of relationship where it's like, David's his own person. He can say whatever he wants. Jason can say whatever he wants. Or do you feel like you have to kind of monitor each other's public persona, if you will? I tend to praise David when he uses good manners sometimes. Because sometimes you're like, I'm not sure how this is going to go. But he had good tact. That was actually a really nice way to put it. Because I know how that could have gone. There's some of that. But it's never like..."], [0, "don't do that i mean very rarely i can't maybe there's a case or two where it's like don't do that that that would be a bad idea but uh i think there's some times when there's a little bit of like pre-discussion on like to what degree do we want to take this maybe there's some of that like i don't know do you think it's fair to do this or do that or say this or say that but still i think you know we all just do our own thing"], [0, "Yeah, there's not a... I mean, maybe it'd be better sometimes. I don't know. But there isn't like a pre-filter. There isn't like an editor that everything passes through. I mean, I barely have one inside my own head. So we don't have one that lives outside of that. And I think, you know what? It's one of those things where..."]], "participants": []}}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["social media", "public persona", "online debate", "criticism", "disagreement", "communication", "business partners", "cofounders", "reputation", "manners", "tact", "self awareness", "humility", "conflict resolution", "groupthink", "accountability"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
