{"timestamp": 1778565489.8133652, "duration_sec": 2.0152945518493652, "validator_hotkey": "5DkzbwTnocecNohGP4aNVcHZfUgx8uA1MGQ4WB1u3kfi78gE", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Welcome to Tech Talk, y'all."], [0, "Hi, and welcome to Tech Talk, y'all. Season 8, Episode 185. I'm Adam Walker. And I'm Sanjay Parik. And listen, we have a great show for you today. But most importantly for me, we actually have four Weird and Wacky articles, which is one of my favorite segments of the show. And I'm very excited about my own tech rec. Sanjay, I know you're excited about it, too. But we're not going to tell you all about that until later. So you're going to have to hold your horses. You're like a huge Weird and Wacky fan, aren't you?"], [0, "I mean, I really get into the weird and wacky articles. Like, it's just fun. It's like treasure. What were you excited about? Because we didn't start weird and wacky at the very beginning. What were you excited about with the show before we had weird and wacky?"], [0, "Well, I mean, that was when, you know, Bitcoin was just going berserk, right? So we talked about Bitcoin literally every single week. So maybe I was pretty excited about Bitcoin at the time, I think. You were excited about Bitcoin? Yeah. I don't think we have any Bitcoin discussions this episode at all. We haven't even talked about Dogecoin really at all either. I mean, it's like..."], [0, "Is that what you, is that how you pronounce it? I believe you pronounce it Dogecoin. I'm pretty sure. And honestly, like I keep seeing art, like every single article title I see about that talks about it being a joke meme cryptocurrency. And I'm like, can we just, can we just, we know that's how it started. Can we just let that go and actually just talk about it as a thing, please? That would be helpful. So."], [0, "So this is not an actual article, but since you've mentioned it, I saw an article about the creator of Dogecoin. Apparently he sold all of his coin a few years ago in order to buy a Honda Civic or something like that to buy a car. So it's probably worth a lot more now than it was."], [0, "I mean, it's gone up by like, what, 2,000% or something just astronomical in the last couple of months. I mean, he is really kicking himself right now. That's the most expensive Honda Civic ever purchased, I think, is what that really is. It's unfortunate because that's going down in value, whereas the coin is maybe going up in value too."], [0, "All right. Well, let's let's dive in. Listen, in this episode, we're going to talk about Verizon. We got to talk about Berkshire Hathaway, Google. We're going to talk about Instagram and Twitter and Apple and Peloton and and and and we're like, so let's just let's dive in. Verizon sells Yahoo and AOL, the private equity firm for five billion dollars. And listen, Sanjay, I would like to know who that private equity firm is because I have a bridge that I need to sell. OK."], [0, "It's a real nice bridge, man. And you can charge by the passenger as they come across it. That's all I'm trying to say. So here's the thing is that Verizon is going to maintain a 10% stake in the company. And it's going to be called Yahoo at the end of it. So the AOL name, I guess, goes away."], [0, "But they spent $9 billion buying all of this. These assets just continue to drop and drop and drop. Like, who in their right mind thinks, hmm, I need to spend $5 billion for Yahoo and AOL because that's going to be money well spent. It's going to gain. Like, come on. Of course it's not going to gain. They've been dying for 15 years. Just let it go. Yeah. And they keep killing off projects too, right? They've become just like Google where..."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Technology"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["technology", "podcast", "cryptocurrency", "bitcoin", "dogecoin", "finance", "investing", "business", "telecom", "mergers", "acquisitions", "private equity", "social media", "big tech", "internet companies"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
