h local housing markets, its impact on community development , and the social equity benefits it promotes."], [2, "Critics say Boston\u2019s inclusionary zoning hurts construction ...\nOct 26, 2025 \u00b7 A year after Boston's inclusionary zoning policy was made more aggressive, developers and politicians have criticized it for hindering housing construction \u2014 but there's more to the story."], [3, "Impact of Rising Interest Rates on Commercial Property ...\nRising interest rates can significantly impact commercial property values by increasing borrowing costs and reducing buyer demand."], [4, "The Interplay Between Cap Rates and Interest Rates\nThe relationship between capitalization rates (cap rates) and interest rates is more nuanced than first meets the eye."], [5, "How Interest Rates Are Shaping Commercial ...\nInterest rates are one of the most influential forces in commercial real estate, shaping how assets are valued, financed, and leased."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": null}, "prompt_chain": null, "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["inclusionary zoning", "affordable housing", "housing policy", "zoning policy", "urban planning", "land use", "real estate development", "municipal government", "massachusetts", "cambridge", "commercial real estate", "interest rates", "mortgage rates", "property valuation", "capitalization rates", "real estate market", "housing construction", "housing supply", "financing costs", "asset pricing"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778580585.0375383, "duration_sec": 6.84996485710144, "validator_hotkey": "5HNe4Yx7idMcgrsoPogLVko2AA8Pap33aNyXQhpwBxsS4H4Q", "task_type": "named_entities_extraction", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "named_entities_extraction", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "document", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "October 22, 2025\nA regular meeting of the City Council of the City of Boston was held in the Christopher A. Iannella\nChamber, City Hall on Wednesday, October 22, 2025 at 12:05 PM.\nPresident Louijeune in the Chair. Present Councilors Breadon, Coletta Zapata, Durkan, FitzGerald,\nFlynn, Mejia, Murphy, Pep\u00e9n, Santana, Weber, and Worrell.\nPastor DeShay Freemyer-Jackson, Brighton-Allston Congregational Church, delivered the invocation,\nand the meeting was opened with the pledge of allegiance.\nThe Chair moved to adopt the minutes from the October 8, 2025 City Council Meeting.\nMotion prevailed.\n_________________________________________________________________________\n1831 Message and order authorizing the City of Boston to accept and expend a\ngrant of One Million Dollars ($1,000,000.00) from the United States\nDepartment of the Interior under the Land and Water Conservation Fund\n(LWCF) Act of 1965 (Pub. L. 88-578, 78 Stat 897), to be administered by\nthe Boston Parks and Recreation Department, f"]], "participants": null}}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "ner_001", "crc": 1321322, "title": "Extract named entities from documents", "name": "extract_named_entities", "description": "Identifies and extracts named entities from provided documents.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "ner", "prompt_template": "Extract all named entities from the provided document. Include the following entity types: PERSON, ORGANIZATION, LOCATION, and any other relevant entities. Return as comma-delimited list of entities with their types (e.g., 'John Smith (PERSON), ACM Corp (ORGANIZATION)). Only return the entities without any additional commentary.", "output_variable": "extracted_entities", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["city council of the city of boston", "city of boston", "boston city hall", "christopher a. iannella chamber", "president louijeune", "councilor breadon", "councilor coletta zapata", "councilor durkan", "councilor fitzgerald", "councilor flynn", "councilor mejia", "councilor murphy", "councilor pep\u00e9n", "councilor santana", "councilor weber", "councilor worrell", "pastor deshay freemyer-jackson", "brighton-allston congregational church", "united states department of the interior", "land and water conservation fund", "land and water conservation fund act of 1965 (pub. l. 88-578)", "boston parks and recreation department", "$1", "000", "000.00"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778581106.3385508, "duration_sec": 2.422203540802002, "validator_hotkey": "5GQyFzvtVMw9X45t6dvUFgR9unFpDCccPPCiAoqJrtPuC8my", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Aber gef\u00e4hrdet ist die Demokratie aktuell st\u00e4rker als in allen anderen etablierten Demokratien. Ein besonders hohes Demokratieniveau sieht der j\u00fcngste BTI in Estland, Lettland und Litauen, aber auch den EU-Beitrittsl\u00e4ndern Albanien und Nordmazedonien sowie in Botswana, Chile, Uruguay oder auch Taiwan. Globale R\u00fcckschritte bei Freiheitsrechten und Wahlen Autokratische Regierungen gehen immer repressiver gegen Opposition, Medien und Zivilgesellschaft vor, hei\u00dft es."], [0, "Verst\u00e4rkt g\u00e4be es digitale \u00dcberwachung. Das Internet werde abgeschaltet, um Kritik und Opposition zu unterdr\u00fccken. In 54 Prozent der untersuchten L\u00e4nder erf\u00fcllen Wahlen denen nach keine demokratischen Mindeststandards, seien oft nur eine Farce."], [0, "In Georgien und Serbien seien Wahlen gravierend manipuliert worden. In Belarus, Russland oder Ruanda h\u00e4tten Wahlergebnisse schon vor der Stimmabgabe festgestanden. Rechtsstaatlichkeit mit Gewaltenteilung und unabh\u00e4ngiger Justiz werden in Autokratien abgebaut oder missachtet. Parlamente w\u00fcrden umgangen. Die Justiz werde behindert. Unabh\u00e4ngige Institutionen w\u00fcrden abgeschafft oder mit Gefolgsleuten besetzt. Die Untersuchung warnt,"], [0, "Auch zahlreiche gew\u00e4hlte Regierungen hebelten gezielt demokratische Kerninstitutionen aus, um ihre Macht zu sichern. Am l\u00e4ngsten und umfassendsten ist diese Entwicklung in Ungarn, sagt Donner. In der Slowakei, in Bulgarien, Indien, Mexiko, Namibia, den Philippinen oder S\u00fcdafrika sei es \u00e4hnlich. In einigen L\u00e4ndern, etwa Georgien, Serbien oder der T\u00fcrkei, h\u00e4tten solche R\u00fcckschritte in eine Autokratie gef\u00fchrt."], [0, "Autorit\u00e4re Regierungen sind anf\u00e4lliger f\u00fcr Korruption, Loyalit\u00e4t werde belohnt, Fr\u00fcnde w\u00fcrden gesichert, schildert Hauke Hartmann, der das BTI-Projekt mitleitet. Zugleich schwinden freier Wettbewerb und Eigentumsrechte, es g\u00e4be ausbeuterische Wirtschaftsstrukturen. Armut und Ungleichheit seien in zwei Dritteln der Autokratien stark ausgepr\u00e4gt. In der Auswertung zeigt sich in vielen L\u00e4ndern ein bemerkenswert lebendiger Widerstand in der Gesellschaft."], [0, "Entschlossene B\u00fcrger setzten sich gegen autorit\u00e4re \u00dcbergriffe zur Wehr, mitunter sogar unter Einsatz des eigenen Lebens, so wie im Iran, unterstreich Donner. Ermutigend, in Bangladesch, Madagaskar oder Sri Lanka f\u00fchrten Proteste zum Sturz autorit\u00e4rer Regierungen. Es gibt keine Erfolgsgarantie daf\u00fcr, dass man autorit\u00e4re Phasen wieder umkehren kann. Aber, auch Autokratien stehen unter Druck."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["News & Politics"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["democracy", "authoritarianism", "political freedom", "elections", "civil rights", "repression", "surveillance", "corruption", "rule of law", "judiciary", "opposition", "media", "civil society", "protests", "inequality"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778581727.4118981, "duration_sec": 2.737135648727417, "validator_hotkey": "5C8LULGoFybR7ybg4S8qQkaaowGXFFja4KmMoSqwhxuAsn33", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[3, "Well, I got them all, you know, I got them all pointed out. I got a report on every single one of them. Which one would you want me to start with? I got\u2014 my competition's everywhere. Everybody's my competition."], [1, "There are dozens of street promoters like Alberto, and because there are so many of them, all working on commission, Alberto's success depends on his charisma. He has to give the best performance. And so Alberto has his own strategies to try to stand out and make a good impression. Besides workshopping comedic material on the job, he told me this one other thing. He tends to play up how American he is. It's not a hard thing for him to do because like many people who grew up along the border, Alberto traveled back and forth a lot. He lived in Arizona but crossed the border weekly. His English is good. He describes himself as being \"from the border.\"."], [3, "So I grew up, you know, going to school and then coming down the weekends down to Mexico. And a lot of kids grew up like that. Because there's a lot of people in Agua Dulce that were\u2014 oh, I forgot to mention I was deported."], [1, "Alberto was deported to Mexico in 2010. In fact, I learned that almost all of Molar City's street promoters are deportees. It is in fact their Americanness, their American English, that makes them ideal candidates for this role."], [3, "It helped me break the ice. It helps me bond with people. Right away they can tell that I lived in America."], [1, "Oh, they bring it up?"], [3, "Yeah, they'll say it like that. They'll be like, \"Oh, I can hear you. Oh yeah, you lived in the States, huh?\" I'm like, \"Yes. Got me a little agent McCasian over there.\" So it makes them\u2014 makes me relate to them more and feel more relaxed."], [1, "Alberto tells me he'll recognize familiar faces crossing into Mexico from time to time. So-and-so from high school, his friend's uncle. But he doesn't get to see his family so often. They all live in Arizona and don't like to come visit."], [3, "They really\u2014 they really only come when they have to."], [1, "Yeah."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Society & Culture"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["immigration", "deportation", "border life", "mexico", "united states", "street marketing", "tourism", "commission work", "sales", "performance", "identity", "language", "family separation", "cross border travel", "cultural assimilation"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
