ut", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["new jersey", "radio", "local identity", "advertising", "clothing", "menswear", "fashion", "comfort", "style", "athleisure", "sweatpants", "jackets", "discount", "online shopping"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778588123.7091346, "duration_sec": 3.2769405841827393, "validator_hotkey": "5GQyFzvtVMw9X45t6dvUFgR9unFpDCccPPCiAoqJrtPuC8my", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "And it's very, very much a book about individuals and people relate to that. But it obviously has this massive implications to the world outside. And at the time of collectivism just having been defeated, fascism and the United States representing individualism has defeated collectivism."], [0, "but where collectivist ideas are still popular in the form of socialism and communism. And for the individual, there's constant struggle between what people tell me to do, what society tells me to do, what my mother tells me to do, and what I think I should do. I think it's unbelievably appealing, particularly to young people who are trying to figure out what they want to do in life, trying to figure out what's important in life."], [0, "it had this enormous appeal. It's romantic. It's bigger than life. The characters are big heroes. It's very American in that sense. It's about individualism. It's about the triumph of individualism. And so I think that's what related. And it had this big romantic element from the... I mean, when I use romantic, I use it kind of in the sense of..."], [0, "movement in art, but it also has this romantic element in the sense of a relationship between a man and a woman that's very intriguing. It's not only that there's a, I would say, almost rape scene, right? I would say, but it's also that this woman is hard to understand. I mean, I've read it more than once and I still can't quite figure out Dominique, right? Because she loves him and she wants to destroy him and she marries other people. I mean, think about that too. Here she's writing a book in the 1940s."], [0, "There's lots of sex. There's a woman who marries more than one person, having sex with more than one person, very unconventional. She's having sex with Rook even though she's not married to Rook. This is 1945."], [0, "And it's very jarring to people. It's very unexpected, but it's also a book of its time. It's about individuals pursuing their passion, pursuing their life, and not caring about convention and what people think, but doing what they think is right. And so I think it's, I encourage everybody to read it, obviously. Yeah."], [0, "So was that the first time she articulated something that sounded like a philosophy of individualism? I mean, the philosophy's there in We the Living, right? Because at the end of the day, the woman is, the hero of We the Living is this individualist stuck in Soviet Union, so she's struggling with these things."], [0, "So the theme is there already. It's not as fleshed out. It's not as articulated philosophically."], [0, "And it's certainly the Enanthem, which is a dystopian novel where this dystopia in the future has \u2013 there's no I. Everything is we. And it's about one guy who breaks out of that. I don't want to give it away, but breaks out of that. So these themes are running \u2013 and then we have \u2013 and they've been published some of the early Ayn Rand stories that she was writing \u2013"], [0, "in preparation for writing her novel, stories she was writing when she first came to America. And you can see these same philosophical elements, even in the male-female relationships and the passion and the, you know, in the conflict, you see them even in those early pieces. And she's just developing them. And the same philosophically, she's developing her philosophy with her literature. And of course, after The Fountainhead,"]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Coding"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["ayn rand", "individualism", "collectivism", "socialism", "communism", "fascism", "political philosophy", "literature", "dystopian fiction", "american culture", "personal freedom", "romance", "sexuality", "feminism", "morality"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778588493.308836, "duration_sec": 4.739961862564087, "validator_hotkey": "5C8LULGoFybR7ybg4S8qQkaaowGXFFja4KmMoSqwhxuAsn33", "task_type": "named_entities_extraction", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "named_entities_extraction", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "document", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Seattle Council Committee Report\nHousing, Arts, and Civil Rights\nCommittee\nCouncil Chamber, City\nWednesday, April 22, 2026, 2:00 PM\nHall\n600 4th Avenue\nSeattle, WA 98104\nThis meeting also constitutes a meeting of the City Council, provided that the meeting shall be conducted as a\ncommittee meeting under the Council Rules and Procedures, and Council action shall be limited to committee\nbusiness.\nPlease Note: Times listed are estimated\nA. Call To Order\nMeeting Start Time: 2:02 p.m.\nPresiding Officer: Chair Foster\nPresent: 4 - Dionne Foster, Eddie Lin, Debora Juarez,Maritza Rivera\nExcused: 1 - Joy Hollingsworth\nLate Arrival: 1 - Alexis Mercedes Rinck\nB. Approval of the Agenda\nC. Public Comment\nD. Items of Business\n1. Appt 03471 Appointment of Amy Nguyen as Director of the Office of Arts and\nCulture.\nThe Committee recommends that City Council confirm the Appointment (Appt).\nIn Favor: 4 - Foster, Lin, Juarez,Rinck\nOpposed: None\n2. Appt 03487 Appointment of Tera Beach as member, Seattle Arts"]], "participants": null}}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "ner_001", "crc": 1321322, "title": "Extract named entities from documents", "name": "extract_named_entities", "description": "Identifies and extracts named entities from provided documents.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "ner", "prompt_template": "Extract all named entities from the provided document. Include the following entity types: PERSON, ORGANIZATION, LOCATION, and any other relevant entities. Return as comma-delimited list of entities with their types (e.g., 'John Smith (PERSON), ACM Corp (ORGANIZATION)). Only return the entities without any additional commentary.", "output_variable": "extracted_entities", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["seattle city council", "housing arts and civil rights committee", "seattle city hall", "council chamber", "600 4th avenue seattle wa 98104", "dionne foster", "eddie lin", "debora juarez", "maritza rivera", "joy hollingsworth", "alexis mercedes rinck", "amy nguyen", "office of arts and culture", "seattle arts", "tera beach"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778588754.5972853, "duration_sec": 2.0646450519561768, "validator_hotkey": "5HNe4Yx7idMcgrsoPogLVko2AA8Pap33aNyXQhpwBxsS4H4Q", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "New Jersey Governor Mikey Sherrill has signed legislation to prevent law enforcement, including ICE agents, from wearing masks. New Jersey is the second state this year to enact a ban on face coverings. The new law also requires officers to present identification prior to arresting or detaining someone."], [0, "The Trump administration is already suing New Jersey over one of Sherrill's executive orders. That order prohibits federal immigration agents from making arrests in non-public areas of state property, such as correctional facilities and courthouses. ICE says its officers wear masks to prevent doxing, adding that agents carry badges and credentials. Washington State's Governor Bob Ferguson signed a similar law banning law enforcement from wearing masks earlier this month."], [0, "Women's Olympic sports will now be limited to females. The International Olympic Committee announcing the new policy aimed at protecting female athletes, while athletes identifying as transgender barred from women's Olympic events."], [0, "All athletes wanting to qualify or take part in women's events at the Games will have to go a gene test to confirm their eligibility. The committee's decision follows gender controversies at the 2024 Olympics in Paris involving two boxers competing in the women's events."], [0, "A year earlier, the International Boxing Association banned both athletes from the World Championships after they failed a gender eligibility test. Both won Olympic gold in their weight classes. Warner Brothers shareholders will vote on its $110 billion merger with Paramount on April 23rd. This brings the companies closer to completing a major deal that could reshape the media landscape."], [0, "Paramount is offering an incentive to Warner Brothers shareholders. A 25 percent share quarterly ticking fee will begin in October. This applies if the deal is not completed by then. Investor approval would move the deal forward but challenges remain. U.S. and European regulators will review it closely. They will check if the merger could raise prices and assess its impact on competition."], [0, "And coming up, the U.S. is presenting a 15-point peace plan to Iran. What President Trump and Special Envoy Steve Whitcoff have to say about the latest negotiations. And a new book exposing the Chinese regime's forced organ harvesting is one of this week's bestsellers. Find out more about Killed to Order by a senior editor of the Epoch Times."], [0, "Welcome back. President Trump and his cabinet giving an update on talks with Iranian leaders. Here they are speaking on Operation Epic Fury during the 11th cabinet meeting of Trump's second term."], [0, "hitting Iran's military capabilities at a level that few people have ever seen before. People never knew there was such a capability. We're the strongest military anywhere in the world, by far. I built it during my first administration, and I used it during my second administration. Unfortunately, because I'd rather not have to use it."], [0, "But it's a display of force and precision and skill like nothing the world has really witnessed, although you got a pretty good witnessing of it in Venezuela also. That was a smaller version of what we're doing now. We're crushing their missiles and drone stockpiles, destroying the defense industrial base. We've wiped out their navy completely."]], "participants": []}}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_