{"timestamp": 1778590706.715073, "duration_sec": 4.380568265914917, "validator_hotkey": "5DkzbwTnocecNohGP4aNVcHZfUgx8uA1MGQ4WB1u3kfi78gE", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "for that leadership position. So taking that position may actually be easier than it seems right now. It may be easier to become the leader of that group. In fact, you could even talk to them about potentially becoming the champion of the coding practices, the best practices for the group. And it's very possible, if not likely, that they will be totally okay with that. In fact, a lot of people appreciate when someone else takes leadership and"], [0, "and provides them with some level of dependability. And John, by assuming that role, you could be lifting some stress off of their shoulders. In fact, if you're doing your job right, hopefully you are lifting some stress off of their shoulders. So remember that it takes effort. Not everyone necessarily wants to be in that job."], [0, "So prepare for other people to actually want you to be the leader and also prepare for it to take a lot of energy. And my final recommendation for you is to beware of the connotation of leadership titles. Beware of the connotation of leadership titles. Remember, your goal isn't to become the dictator first."], [0, "over the group of developers that you're working with. But instead, your goal is to institute learning and best practices. You want to facilitate good communication between the stakeholders and the developers of the product. You want to make sure that developers are documenting their work"], [0, "for example, with sufficient detail about their decisions. You want the code to follow common design patterns so that refactoring down the road is much, much easier. You want to make sure developers on your team are aware of the most important factors"], [0, "of a given project, the most important decision-making factors, the timeline, the budget, those kinds of things, that's going to fall on your shoulders to make sure that the developers are aware of those kinds of things. Trying to attain a title can sometimes come with apprehension from the people that you are leading."], [0, "The connotations of titles that come along with leadership can sometimes suggest that the leader is now dictating every step and every keystroke that I make and that you're looking over my shoulder as the leader. But you must be very clear about this in the process and explain that your intention is to support the team, to serve them and make them a stronger unit."], [0, "and to facilitate best practices, and to encourage learning and constant adaptation, in your case, Jean, as Android developers, to become better Android developers, to become better Java developers, to understand the underlying technology, and to truly enjoy the craftsmanship of"], [0, "of being an Android developer. So that is your job as a leader is to uncover those things that make your team better, not to be the overlord, but instead to be the support system to enable that team. And if your team understands that, then instead of seeing the connotations of the leadership titles, they will see you as a friend and a confidant"], [0, "And they will see you as someone who is making their job better, making their life better by creating these systems that make their work sufficiently better. Thank you so much for listening to today's episode of Developer Tea. John, I hope that this was an interesting discussion for you. And I hope that this kind of provides some context around how I think about leadership. There are a lot of"]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Coding"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "