{"timestamp": 1778591954.34517, "duration_sec": 1.9233314990997314, "validator_hotkey": "5HNe4Yx7idMcgrsoPogLVko2AA8Pap33aNyXQhpwBxsS4H4Q", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "This audio is presented by Hacker Noon, where anyone can learn anything about any technology. The 7 Best Co-Parenting Apps in 2026, by Steve Byatt. If your stomach drops every time your phone buzzes with a message from your ex, you're not alone. For many divorced and separated parents, co-parenting isn't just about schedules and school pickups."], [0, "It's about managing tone, documenting conversations, protecting yourself legally, and trying not to let conflict spill over onto your children. One misunderstood text can spiral into an argument. One hostile message can derail your entire day. One missing record can become a courtroom headache. And yet, you still have to communicate. That's why choosing the best co-parenting app matters more than ever in 2026."], [0, "The right app doesn't just organize your calendar, it protects your peace, your credibility, and your child stability. Let's find the app that makes co-parenting feel more manageable, more organized, and easier to navigate day-to-day. 7 Best Co-Parenting Apps Compared 1. Best Interest Best for Peace, AI Safety, and Budget The modern choice, Best Interest takes a different approach than traditional co-parenting apps by focusing on communication safety and conflict prevention."], [0, "Instead of simply documenting problems, it helps prevent them by using AI to filter hostile messages, guide comma responses, and keep communication child-centered. Best interest is built for real-life co-parenting and everyday communication challenges."], [0, "How it supports your co-parenting filters Hostile incoming messages Best interest uses AI to screen incoming messages and block or summarize hostile, manipulative, or off-topic language before you see it. This helps prevent emotional triggers and keeps communication focused on information that actually matters. Reviews messages before you send them AI reviews your outgoing messages and suggests calmer, more neutral phrasing when something could escalate conflict."], [0, "You stay in control of what you send, but with an extra layer of protection for your tone and record. Works even if your co-parent will not join, you can use best interest on your own to draft, analyze, and send messages through the app while keeping your personal number private. This makes it possible to get support and documentation without needing your co-parent's cooperation. Creates court-ready communication records, messages and journal entries are timestamped, unalterable, and exportable."], [0, "This provides reliable documentation if you ever need records for mediation, court, or professional support. Helps organize day-to-day parenting responsibilities, shared or private tasks, reminders, and notes make it easier to track appointments, school deadlines, and handoffs. This reduces misunderstandings and mental load. Integrated AI Co-Parenting Coach A specialized AI agent helps you with co-parenting questions, reviewing messages, even reads and understands your parenting plan in context."], [0, "Included in the free plan. Pros helps reduce anxiety around co-parent communication. Does not require both parents to participate. Use without a court order. Accessible for budget-conscious parents. Prioritizes emotional safety alongside documentation. Designed for real-world co-parenting, not just court cases. Free version available with unlimited messaging and AI coaching. Cons newer platform than legacy apps."], [0, "Fewer built-in financial and expense tools than some competitors. Ideal for parents who feel drained by hostile communication and want built-in protection, not just a record of what was said. 2. Our Family Wizard best for court orders, the old school standard. Our Family Wizard is one of the longest-running co-parenting apps and is widely recognized by family courts. It is built primarily around documentation, records, and accountability rather than conflict prevention."], [0, "For parents whose judge specifically orders this platform, or who want a familiar, court-accepted name, our family wizard remains a common choice."]], "participants": []}}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["coparenting", "parenting", "divorce", "family law", "child custody", "communication", "messaging", "mobile apps", "scheduling", "conflict resolution", "artificial intelligence", "emotional safety", "legal documentation", "court records", "privacy"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778592571.2758937, "duration_sec": 3.188732147216797, "validator_hotkey": "5DkzbwTnocecNohGP4aNVcHZfUgx8uA1MGQ4WB1u3kfi78gE", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[3, "Genau, also ich bin Paul, einer der Mitgr\u00fcnder von Vestigas. Wir sind eine Supply-Chain-Plattform in der Bauindustrie, jetzt gerade gro\u00df, 8 Billionen geraced, haben letztes Jahr super starkes Wachstum mit 10 Acquisitions hingelegt und sind da sehr, sehr froh dr\u00fcber. Und freut mich auch, hier zu sein, \u00fcber Instafford zu reden."], [0, "Genau, Instafford hat uns zusammengebracht, ist unser Partner, und du kennst sie auch gut. Ihr nutzt sie schon l\u00e4nger, ne?"], [3, "Absolut, also jetzt seit ein bisschen mehr als einem Jahr im Einsatz und bald 15 Leute dar\u00fcber geheuert, sowohl Tech als auch Sales als auch andere Bereiche. Und ein super spannender Weg, weil es gerade so eine stark kuratierte Plattform ist. Das hei\u00dft gute Leute, die auch alle auf Suche sind, und das habe ich halt eigentlich nirgendwo sonst."], [0, "Also ich h\u00f6re raus, rundum empfehlenswert. Absolut."], [3, "Mit 15 von unseren bald 40 Leuten haben wir dann auch sehr, sehr viele gute Leute dar\u00fcber bekommen. Deswegen, ich kann es nur empfehlen."], [0, "Paul, dann lieben Dank und weiterhin viel Erfolg."], [3, "Vielen, vielen Dank dir. Ciao, ciao."], [0, "Ja, und f\u00fcr alle, die Instaffo mal ausprobieren m\u00f6chten, unter instaffo.com/insider k\u00f6nnt ihr die Software testen und bekommt auch noch einen Willkommensrabatt in H\u00f6he von 500 \u20ac. Glaubst du denn, aber ich meine, zum Plankensetzen br\u00e4uchtest du ja irgendjemanden, der versteht, was da gerade vor sich geht, auf einer internationalen Ebene mitreden kann, wei\u00dft du? Also ich \u00fcberlege gerade, wer kann die Planken setzen, weil das k\u00f6nnen ja jetzt keine Regierungen sein oder so."], [1, "Nee, ich glaube, das ist so ein ganz klassischer Fall von ab einem gewissen Zeitpunkt der Maturity der Technologie selber reguliert sich das in gewisser Weise. Was wir ja aktuell sehen, ist, jeder probiert aus, was, also wie extrem es geht und wie stark man das im Prinzip vorantreiben kann. Es wird ja h\u00e4ufig durch den freien Markt schon anders adaptiert und reguliert, wenn du so m\u00f6chtest, also nicht durch den Gesetzgeber reguliert, sondern durch den Markt reguliert, einfach dadurch, dass jetzt beispielsweise ja auch, vielleicht war das ja auch einer der Punkte, die diskutiert wurden bei OpenClaw, er kann es halt selber nicht mehr in der Sicherheit irgendwie garantieren und auf den Status bringen, auf den man es im Prinzip br\u00e4uchte, um das Ganze auch perspektivisch nicht nur dem Privatanwender zur Verf\u00fcgung zu stellen, sondern f\u00fcr Unternehmen im Prinzip sinnhaft nutzbar zu machen. Und da ist nat\u00fcrlich schon etwas, ich glaube, da wirst du einfach verschiedene Abstufungen von Autonomie von so einem Agent sehen, um einfach einzelne klar definierte Use Cases im Prinzip autonom und vielleicht auch sich selbst verbessernd irgendwie abzubilden, aber nicht notwendigerweise diese aktuelle Tendenz, alles so extrem wie m\u00f6glich autonom zu gestalten. Ja, also selbst zur\u00fcckkommend auf unsere Einleitung im Prinzip, wenn ich jetzt nur auf mich selber schaue. Ich bin ja auch daran interessiert, dass ich jetzt nicht einfach nur frei irgendwelche Daten von m\u00f6glichen Mandanten und Kunden und Startups frei durch die Welt schicke und dann irgendwelche LLMs damit machen lasse. Also das mache ich halt dann einmal und dann habe ich ein Riesenproblem im Zweifel, wenn es mal falsch l\u00e4uft. Und das ist nat\u00fcrlich etwas, wo man schon drauf aufpassen muss. Und deswegen sage ich, das reguliert sich im Zweifel Use Case f\u00fcr Use Case irgendwo selber."], [0, "Ja, du sprichst gerade vom freien Markt, ne? Ich finde das ganz spannend. Wir reden ja, glaube ich, gerade vom SARS-Get-On oder so \u00e4hnlich hei\u00dft es, glaube ich, ne? Also wir reden davon, dass die SARS-Branche gerade irgendwie komplett unter Beschuss steht und unter Wasser ist, auch an der B\u00f6rse und so weiter. Ich frage mich, ob jetzt hier schon die n\u00e4chste Welle eingel\u00e4utet wird und dann vielleicht sogar die KI-Modelle, die LLMs, schon wieder umdenken m\u00fcssten, weil jetzt der n\u00e4chste Kontrahent um die Ecke kommt, ne, und was Neues erfindet. Also, ich komme mit dieser Taktung gerade gar nicht, ich komme nicht mehr hinterher, jetzt durchzudringen, was denn jetzt eigentlich so ein Open Claw hinterher f\u00fcr die Wirtschaft bedeutet."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Business"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["artificial intelligence", "large language models", "autonomous agents", "technology regulation", "market dynamics", "data privacy", "cybersecurity", "enterprise software", "saas industry", "venture funding", "startup growth", "recruitment", "supply chain", "construction industry", "mergers and acquisitions"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778592707.3587759, "duration_sec": 2.5215983390808105, "validator_hotkey": "5GQyFzvtVMw9X45t6dvUFgR9unFpDCccPPCiAoqJrtPuC8my", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "And anyway, I've really, really been enjoying it. It's funny because, you know, I mentioned the swearing. The swearing isn't as frequent in this one. But the content and feel is a little bit darker. But yeah, really, really enjoyed that. So if you're looking for a good fiction, definitely check it out."], [0, "And then I've been playing with a few tools that I've really been enjoying. One that I'm looking forward to diving into some is Metabase. And Metabase is a system you can use to connect to a database. So since I've been working on this podcasting app, and I'm hoping to have it released, do a general availability like AJ just did, or maybe beta."], [0, "I'd like to start tracking some of the stuff in it. And Metabase connects to your database and gives you nice visual views into what your app is doing. And so I'm really looking forward to digging into that. It is open source and you can just click a couple of buttons and deploy it to Heroku. So definitely check that out. Gil, what are your picks?"], [0, "Lots of them I'll have to choose. Okay, this is for my wife, Cat Zero. It's a scientific thriller, if you want. The lead person is a scientist, a woman scientist in academia. The thriller part isn't very thrilling, I have to admit. But for me, my wife is a physicist in academia, so it gave me some insight and insight."], [0, "I do talk to her, but some other insight into women in academia and the struggle and the things they have to cope with on a day-to-day basis. Obviously, a lot of those things are relevant to women in high-tech and in software development. There are similarities in that case."], [0, "But it's really well written. It's written by a woman. You can feel that. And it really gave me the perspective about the whole issue of women in workplaces and women in academia specifically. So I recommend this highly, Cat Zero. It's written well. Another really strange book."], [0, "It's called The Origin of Consciousness in the Becameral Mind, which is a strange title. It's a theory written by, I think, a sociologist or psychologist. It's a theory that humankind did not develop consciousness until after..."], [0, "or during the Greek age, so like 1000 BC. Before that, we were not conscious at all. And consciousness also developed in different ways at different times in different parts of the globe."], [0, "And, you know, you start by this is a weird theory. No way. And the writer convinces you piece by piece that it may be true. And through a lot of chapters, you say either it's totally, totally wrong or the guy is on to something."], [0, "And it's not the theory itself, but the way it changed how I think about the way we act and the way we feel, how much of it is conscious and how much of it isn't. And starting to understand that most of what we do, even things that we think of as conscious stuff, actually isn't. It's going on in the back of our minds. So that was a huge, huge, huge eye opener for me. Nice. People want to find you online. Where do they go?"]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Coding"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["books", "fiction", "thriller", "science", "academia", "women", "workplace", "software development", "data analytics", "databases", "open source", "app development", "psychology", "consciousness", "human behavior"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778593429.256541, "duration_sec": 2.699824094772339, "validator_hotkey": "5DkzbwTnocecNohGP4aNVcHZfUgx8uA1MGQ4WB1u3kfi78gE", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "I might as well just put whatever. No, no. I'm serious. Like, I feel like the cell, like the grass would, would, would do a real damage to it. No. Okay. So then the other weird thought that I just had was like, so you've got this car that's got all this hair on it. But like, what if you have to shave it? Like what if it keeps growing? That's some new technology. I'm just curious to see. Just grows hair from the sun. See this a week after they installed it. You know, I'm sure it's not going to look so fluffy and. Especially if it gets wet. Yeah. No."], [0, "Like a gross teddy bear. No, that thing's going to live inside somewhere. Mm-hmm. Yeah, there's going to be in a kid zone or something. Yeah, so that's the, I guess you could call it the wrap of the week. It's, you know, we've talked about it many times, the creativity of people. And, I mean, I have to, you know, give them a tip of my cap as, you know, it seems like it's a nod to the, you know, Dumb and Dumber days. So I love that. Yeah."], [0, "I dig it. Same here. It's got that Highland cow. I want to go up and pet it. Right now when it's clean, not later when it's dirty. I want to go hug you. I just want to give it a hug. Other than that, that's all I got, guys. Appreciate everybody who came out."], [0, "Jumped into chat. Tess Latino joined us tonight. So appreciate him. I would love to get him on the pod just to talk to him about some of this stuff. Maybe we could hear the road stories. Yeah. Yeah. I would love that. Thank you guys. Appreciate you. Thank you everyone that joined us in chat. We'll see you guys next week."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Technology"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["cars", "vehicle wrap", "car customization", "novelty design", "artificial fur", "hair growth", "technology", "sunlight", "creativity", "pop culture", "comedy film", "dumb and dumber", "cleanliness", "podcast"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778593484.2627654, "duration_sec": 3.3262240886688232, "validator_hotkey": "5DkzbwTnocecNohGP4aNVcHZfUgx8uA1MGQ4WB1u3kfi78gE", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Hello and welcome to Keep On Cybertruckin', a podcast where Cybertruck owners share their experiences, talk about all things EVs and technology and apparently the Grinch. But we have Chase and we kind of have Will here. I'm here, I promise. I'm eating a pizza. Nobody's here to look at my face. We'll be fine. He's here with us. So let's get into that, Chase. You brought up right before we went live that you have a beef with the Grinch. Please share."], [0, "Yeah, I put it up on my Twitter. It's kind of a cool thing we did over the weekend. Ended up renting a Cybertruck off Turo from another guy that I know that rents here in Austin. It happened to be a Cyber Beast, but the real reason why we rented it is to go to the Peppermint Parkway, which is like a big festival that they put at the Circuit of America's track."], [0, "And so it's kind of like it's a drive through kind of experience. So you see all the lights as you're driving through because they take you like underneath the tunnel, like kind of inside the track and then outside the track. And then what's cool about it and the reason why we rented the Cybertruck is that you actually get to take a lap around the track too, which is really cool. So this in the Peppermint Parkway was your first get in there. You barely can see in the video unless you have to like zoom in is the Grinch as we like drove by him."], [0, "He looks over at me, he's like, how much you pay for this piece of junk? And I'm like, okay, that's funny. Yeah, you know, I have a funny story. So..."], [0, "My goddaughter, she's always, like, she loves the Grinch, right? So for every Christmas, she wants to watch Grinch movies. She loves the Grinch, all that. My sister took her to Universal Studios, and they had the Grinch there. Well, the Grinch, like you're saying, he's got a little attitude, right? And she knows this, but, you know."], [0, "So he starts like just giving her the hardest time. She started crying. She wanted nothing to do with the Grinch. Now, if you ask her about the Grinch, she's just like, whatever. I want nothing to do with that guy. So, yeah, he's he's not meant to be the nicest guy in the world, you know? So, yeah, I guess this is what is it? The first act Grinch, if you're following along with the live action movie, because like obviously he gets a big heart in the end. Yeah, it depends on which Grinch you can see."], [0, "But it was really cool. I think, if anything, I was also selfishly just wanting to try to drive a Cyber Beast. And so how did you feel about that? I'm going to show your launch here. So it was very rainy that day, so we really couldn't do a whole lot of fun stuff on the road. But we did find a stretch in the neighborhood that was pretty dead. And I took my neighbor and we launched it. And he almost smacked his phone in his face because it..."], [0, "It torqued us so hard. Oh, yeah. Which, it's crazy. Like, it is, like, stupid fast in, like, beast mode. I feel like that's the joy of Tesla that's been there for the last 10 years has been just absolutely pummeling somebody into the seat of a car. I'm like, yeah, so this is launch mode."], [0, "It's phenomenal. The thing about that is the Beast is 845 horsepower. The quad motor large battery Rivian that we have is 835 horsepower. There's a significant difference between the takeoff between those two motors. It's just as..."], [0, "fast by horsepower's sake, but the launch rate is significant in the Teslas. I don't know what it is, but those engines are always ready, whereas Rivian, you have a weird ramp-up into it where it's like"]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Technology"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["cybertruck", "tesla", "electric vehicles", "automotive", "pickup trucks", "car rental", "road trip", "festival", "christmas", "grinch", "theme parks", "driving experience", "acceleration", "horsepower", "rivian"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778594709.0133789, "duration_sec": 3.723367214202881, "validator_hotkey": "5HNe4Yx7idMcgrsoPogLVko2AA8Pap33aNyXQhpwBxsS4H4Q", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "O economista Newton Marques chamou aten\u00e7\u00e3o tamb\u00e9m para o risco de o Tesouro dar aval a esse empr\u00e9stimo, ainda mais sem a divulga\u00e7\u00e3o do balan\u00e7o do BRB. Se o BRB n\u00e3o pagar, quem vai pagar \u00e9 o Tesouro. Ent\u00e3o por isso \u00e9 que o Tesouro tem que fazer algum tipo de exig\u00eancia caso corra esse risco de ter que pagar esse empr\u00e9stimo que n\u00e3o for honrado pelo BRB."], [0, "E com rela\u00e7\u00e3o ao problema que eu vejo maior do BRB \u00e9 que o BRB n\u00e3o publicou seu balan\u00e7o. A gente n\u00e3o sabe realmente quais s\u00e3o as necessidades que o banco tem. E tem mais nessa crise do BRB, hein? Funcion\u00e1rios do Banco de Bras\u00edlia relatam epis\u00f3dios que classificam como ass\u00e9dio moral praticados pelo ex-presidente do banco, Paulo Henrique Costa. Ele que est\u00e1 preso, foi preso em abril na quarta fase da Opera\u00e7\u00e3o Compliance Zero."], [0, "Os relatos descrevem situa\u00e7\u00f5es recorrentes de constrangimento em reuni\u00f5es internas, cobran\u00e7as consideradas excessivas e comportamentos que teriam provocado medo e humilha\u00e7\u00e3o entre servidores desde o in\u00edcio da gest\u00e3o. As informa\u00e7\u00f5es est\u00e3o sendo analisadas pelos \u00f3rg\u00e3os competentes."], [0, "Seguimos com a economia para voc\u00ea saber que o Comit\u00ea de Pol\u00edtica Monet\u00e1ria do Banco Central reduziu a taxa Selic em 0,25 ponto percentual, como j\u00e1 esperava o mercado. Com o segundo corte consecutivo, a taxa caiu de 14,75% para 14,5% ao ano. A decis\u00e3o foi influenciada pela guerra no Ir\u00e3, que provocou aumento no pre\u00e7o do petr\u00f3leo e risco inflacion\u00e1rio no mundo todo."], [0, "No comunicado, o comit\u00ea cita a indefini\u00e7\u00e3o do conflito no Oriente M\u00e9dio, a infla\u00e7\u00e3o acima da meta e fala em cautela, sem sinalizar os pr\u00f3ximos passos. Para o analista da Valor Investimentos, Daniel Teles Barbosa, o cen\u00e1rio de incerteza deixa pouco espa\u00e7o para novos cortes na taxa Selic. O mercado trabalha ainda com uma Selic terminal, alguns mais otimistas."], [0, "sinalizando corte de mais 1% durante esse ano, outros sinalizam mais 0,25%. O fato \u00e9 que agora os dados, principalmente a infla\u00e7\u00e3o provocada por conta do conflito, vai ter que ser muito bem analisado. Nos Estados Unidos, o Fed decidiu manter a taxa de juros no patamar entre 3,5% e 3,75% pela terceira vez seguida."], [0, "E ainda falando de economia, o ministro do Trabalho e Emprego, Luiz Marinho, falou que o uso de recursos do Fundo de Garantia do Tempo de Servi\u00e7o, o FGTS, para o pagamento de d\u00edvidas, no \u00e2mbito daquele programa que est\u00e1 sendo chamado de Desenrola 2.0, ser\u00e1 limitado a 20% do saldo total da conta do FGTS."], [0, "E, al\u00e9m disso, a permiss\u00e3o para o uso do fundo na quita\u00e7\u00e3o de d\u00edvidas vai valer s\u00f3 para trabalhadores com renda de at\u00e9 cinco sal\u00e1rios m\u00ednimos. Representa a\u00ed cerca de R$ 8.100. No caso de trabalhadores que n\u00e3o sejam benefici\u00e1rios do FGTS, haver\u00e1 o parcelamento da d\u00edvida de uma outra forma."], [0, "Segundo o Marinho, o programa ser\u00e1 o foco do pronunciamento que o presidente Lula vai fazer hoje \u00e0 noite em rede nacional em refer\u00eancia ao dia do trabalho, que \u00e9 amanh\u00e3. E as medidas ser\u00e3o detalhadas na semana que vem. Deixa eu chamar a aten\u00e7\u00e3o aqui sua para um dos destaques do Jornal Globo de hoje..."], [0, "que \u00e9 a sa\u00fade dos brasileiros. Saiu uma pesquisa do Instituto Genial Quest que mostra que mais da metade da popula\u00e7\u00e3o brasileira n\u00e3o pratica nenhuma atividade f\u00edsica. Esse levantamento foi conduzido entre os dias 6 e 9 de mar\u00e7o, com 2.004 pessoas de 16 anos ou mais."]], "participants": []}}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["brazil economy", "central bank", "interest rates", "inflation", "monetary policy", "public finance", "government guarantee", "banking regulation", "financial transparency", "corruption investigation", "workplace harassment", "oil prices", "consumer debt", "labor policy", "public health"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
