{"timestamp": 1778624429.1816695, "duration_sec": 3.044889450073242, "validator_hotkey": "5FZe9Mpo5dLXfhGZ4VjRnw6dmz9LVPp6nzqPyDfaS9BLKs33", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[3, "They really\u2014 they really only come when they have to."], [1, "Yeah."], [3, "The reason they don't like it is because of the immigration, the way they treat them when they're crossing. They always get harassed. Yeah. When they're going back to America, they get harassed. So they get tired of that."], [1, "Los Algodones has long been set up for the benefit of Americans, and the journey Americans take to cross into Molar City has always been a simple one. But of course, the journey in the opposite direction is much more complicated. Can I ask you a question that might sound\u2014 I don't know, I don't know how you'll take it, but I'll ask it anyway. You can tell me how you react to it. I've heard from Americans and Canadians, like people describing what it's like to go down to Los Algodones, and people describe just walking freely through the border, like just 5 minutes, no need to even show a passport. And I, I'm just curious what that's like for you on your end, knowing that you were kicked out, and yet part of your job is to interact daily with I don't know, hundreds of people who just walk so freely across this border, you know?"], [3, "The way I see it is like this. Since I am from the border and we lived in America, we went to school in America, what happens is that when I see people coming from America and I see myself that I can't go back, which is like literally Right there, I can see my mom's house from right here."], [1, "Oh, wow."], [3, "That's the hardest thing to see. I see my house. I got the Colorado River, and I can literally see the water tank at the reservation, and then I can see all the way to the Yuma hospital on 24th Street, and then I kind of know more or less where my mom's house is over here. If I had a drone, I could fly it over there and and look at and go, \"Ouch.\"."], [1, "Yeah."], [3, "That's how close I am. That's not easy. It's very hard for me."], [1, "It's 5:00 AM in Algodones. The sky is still dark, not quite sunrise, and Alberto is shuffling around the house, getting ready for for work. The streets are mostly quiet at this hour, just the sound of other promoters and vendors setting up, setting the stage for Molar City. By 6:00 AM, he's at his post. The border opens and the Americans descend. They walk in the shadow of the 30-foot wall that divides them. Crossing the very threshold Alberto cannot."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Society & Culture"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["border crossing", "immigration", "harassment", "travel restrictions", "deportation", "mexican border town", "americans abroad", "daily work", "family separation", "longing for home", "geographic proximity", "border wall", "indigenous reservation", "colorado river", "dental tourism", "north america", "inequality", "human rights"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778624821.5602822, "duration_sec": 4.555598974227905, "validator_hotkey": "5GQyFzvtVMw9X45t6dvUFgR9unFpDCccPPCiAoqJrtPuC8my", "task_type": "webpage_metadata_generation", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "webpage_metadata_generation", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "webpage_markdown", "data": {"window": [[0, "Attempts to reactivate Charlestown\u2019s Pier 5 resumed with the choice of a local nonprofit that sponsors sailing and enrichment programs for 1,000 youths annually as developer.\n\nCourageous Sailing Center for Youth is proposing to rebuild the pier to support a new $73 million educational and community center and \u201camphibious park\u201d designed with resiliency measures to withstand rising sea levels. A 29,500 square-foot building on the rebuilt pier would include classrooms for marine science programs, a theater and a Great Hall for meetings and events.\n\nThe nonprofit has begun a fundraising campaign with the goal of raising $20 million in donations in the next year, which could include naming rights for the former World War II-era ship repair jetty.\n\nThe Boston Planning & Development Agency board approved a tentative developer designation to Courageous Sailing following a presentation at Thursday\u2019s meeting.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s ambitious,\u201d board member Ted Landsmark said. \u201cIt\u2019s innovative. It meets a lot of"], [0, "Understanding Cost Estimation for Marine Construction Projects\nSkilled labor is essential for marine construction projects, and labor costs can vary depending on the availability of skilled workers and labor market conditions. Specialized equipment, such as dredgers, cranes, and pile drivers, is necessary for marine construction projects. The cost of renting or purchasing this equipment adds to project ..."], [1, "Charlestown Pier 5 Approved for Major Redevelopment\nCharlestown \u2019s long-vacant Pier 5 is officially moving forward. On December 12, 2025, the Boston Planning & Development Agency ( BPDA ) awarded tentative designation to Courageous Sailing, clearing the way for a transformative public waterfront redevelopment project in the Charlestown Navy Yard. The proposal marks the first major step toward converting the deteriorated pier into a world-class ..."], [2, "ARCH572 Revitalizing Pier 5 - ArcGIS StoryMaps\nAug 14, 2025 \u00b7 The Boston Planning & Development Agency ( BPDA ) held a virtual community meeting on July 24, 2025, regarding Pier 5 in the Charlestown Navy Yard. The purpose of this meeting was for proponents to the Request for Proposals (RFP) for Pier 5 to present a summary of their proposals and answer questions."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": null}, "prompt_chain": null, "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["waterfront redevelopment", "real estate development", "urban planning", "boston", "charlestown", "navy yard", "harbor revitalization", "harbor infrastructure", "coastal infrastructure", "climate resilience", "sea level rise", "public space", "public parks", "community development", "waterfront access", "pier restoration", "site revitalization", "historic preservation", "marina facilities", "sailing programs"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778626031.0886605, "duration_sec": 2.084709644317627, "validator_hotkey": "5GQyFzvtVMw9X45t6dvUFgR9unFpDCccPPCiAoqJrtPuC8my", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "This episode is brought to you by our friends at GitLab. GitLab is inviting you to attend GitLab Commit 2021, their upcoming user community event August 3rd and 4th. It's free, it's virtual, and everyone can attend. Learn more about modern DevOps and how it transforms companies of all sizes and pushes teams to drive innovation to market. During this two-day conference, attendees across all time zones will learn how they can instill modern DevOps practices at their organizations through in-depth trainings and workshops."], [0, "hear firsthand stories from some of the most well-known companies, and gain insight into cutting-edge CICD and security technologies that bring companies to the next level. Get ready to innovate together during this free event designed to help you to commit to better DevOps. Register and learn more at GitLabCommitVirtual2021.com. Once again, that's GitLabCommitVirtual2021.com. Or check for links in the show notes."], [0, "What was like a difficult thing you remember from the design process? Is there anything that stands out as tricky or contentious or something that really took time to get to grips with? You don't have the name names. I think that f.fuzz function took a lot of thought. Just like the basic structure of it."], [0, "you know, deciding whether or not it was going to be, you know, because the original design, like the original, original, like when I was first writing this out and like talking about it with Flippo and some other people who have been thinking about fuzzing for a while, it looked very similar to what GoFuzz looks like. I don't think there's anything wrong with GoFuzz, but that was what it looked like. It had a fuzz through with a testing on F and then it would just run what was in there. And it was kind of just a continuation of their work. And then, you know, we were just thinking like, but what about all these other things we want to do? Like, is this going to work?"], [0, "And I was like, okay, well, maybe we can do something a little bit different. Maybe we can have it be more clear that this is what is running the fuzzing and then having people allow them to do some pre-work above it as needed. And then that's when we were like, well, maybe this f.fuzz. And then maybe rather than have f.fuzz take a testing.f, we just have to take a testing.t. And that was kind of a later decision. At first, f.fuzz took a testing.f. And then we're like, well,"], [0, "it's doing everything that a unit test does. So why can't it just take a testing.t? And it's like, oh, that's better. And then it started to kind of come together in that way. But that took a lot of time and a lot of thought on how to work through that. Yeah, that's very interesting. And it's also quite interesting that the fuzz method... No, it's a function, isn't it? No, it's a method, isn't it? On the testing... It's a method. It's a method on testing.t. Yeah. I just want to be correct for our pedantic listeners. We do have a few pedantics that we'll write in."], [0, "I say the wrong one often. Yeah. Okay. So it's a function. I've done it wrong again. It's a method. I call it the f.fuz function because I just think it's useful that way. I don't know. Go developers often don't use the word method. They kind of are functions as well, aren't they? That's the thing. They just have a receiver. So in a way, the pedants can do one."], [0, "But that fuzz thing, it takes an empty interface, but it expects a function. So this is quite interesting. And this is kind of like, I think, something that is a little bit unusual. And why is that? Why does it take an interface instead of a typed function?"], [0, "So if it takes an interface, it lets you pass in any kind of function you want. And we have this restriction now that whatever you pass to f.add has to match the type of the fuzz function. So if you f.add a bunch of strings..."], [0, "then your fuzz function must take a string. And we verify that at runtime with reflection. And same, if it takes a string in an integer, then it needs to be a string in the integer and so on. And we also, we can't do it entirely statically either. We talked a while ago about"]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Coding"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["devops", "gitlab", "virtual conference", "user community", "workshops", "devops training", "continuous integration", "security technology", "fuzz testing", "api design", "go programming", "software testing", "reflection", "static typing", "runtime validation", "programming language", "innovation", "decision making"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778626486.5857074, "duration_sec": 2.2309961318969727, "validator_hotkey": "5DkzbwTnocecNohGP4aNVcHZfUgx8uA1MGQ4WB1u3kfi78gE", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "The time is now 7.02am in New York. I'm Noah Levi and this is the latest Israel Today. Ongoing war report."], [0, "In Operation Lion's raw satellite imagery shows tunnel entrances hit and runway access blocked at the Eagle 44 base, a secret Iranian underground air base near the Strait of Hormuz. The site, revealed in 2023, is said to house jets and drones underground."], [0, "and the imagery depicts the entrances and the runway as damaged, likely trapping aircraft inside. In U.S. military role, the blockade related to the Strait of Hormuz was set to begin at 10 a.m. Eastern Time, and targets ships entering or exiting Iranian ports, a plan that differs from pledges to block all vessels entering or leaving the strait itself. The move could extend to other Iranian ports such as Jask or Chabaha, and its effectiveness remains uncertain."], [0, "The United States has deployed additional Navy vessels to the strait, and the broader regional picture includes a ceasefire announced on April 8 that prompted resumed flights and economic activity. Separately, oil markets reacted, with prices rising above $103,"], [0, "a barrel after the blockade was announced, underscoring how the move could affect regional trade and energy markets. In the conflict with Iran and its regional proxies, the IDF said that after completing its operation against Hezbollah in Bint Jabil in southern Lebanon in the coming days, major fights in the area would largely end."], [0, "Clearing operations to remove Hezbollah weapons found during the invasion could continue for a longer period, and there may be limited clashes with leftover Hezbollah forces in parts of southern Lebanon that have not withdrawn north of the Letani River. The broader posture has shifted toward preventing real-time rocket threats to Israel's home front, with air strikes focusing on immediate threats rather than deeper Hezbollah capabilities. In Israeli domestic politics,"], [0, "A Hebrew University poll shows most Israelis oppose the Iran ceasefire and are divided on whether to uphold it, with support for Prime Minister Netanyahu at 34% now, down from 40% at the war's start. In anti-Semitism and anti-Jewish hate, an opinion piece argues Europe failed the test of the Shoah and may be failing again to confront absolute evil."], [0, "noting that remembrance on Yom HaShoah carries heavy weight, while antisemitism persists across far-right and far-left currents, and in Islamist networks. Separately, the International Christian Embassy Jerusalem condemned an Easter ceremony in El Burgo, southern Spain, where a seven-metre effigy depicting Prime Minister Netanyahu was burned."], [0, "calling the act antisemitic and urging the catholic church to address what it describes as one-sided criticism of israel the organization cited similar incidents in other countries and tied the statements to broader concerns about antisemitism"], [0, "In uplifting news, International Good Deeds Day continues to grow, with 115 countries and millions of participants taking part in 2026. Initiated by businesswoman and philanthropist Shari Arison 20 years ago, the day features hundreds of thousands of volunteer projects worldwide."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["News & Politics"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["israel iran conflict", "operation lion", "satellite imagery", "underground air base", "strait of hormuz", "naval blockade", "us navy deployment", "oil prices", "hezbollah", "southern lebanon", "israeli politics", "antisemitism", "energy markets", "maritime security", "public opinion polling", "european politics", "religious tensions", "volunteerism"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778627339.9958198, "duration_sec": 4.845651149749756, "validator_hotkey": "5HNe4Yx7idMcgrsoPogLVko2AA8Pap33aNyXQhpwBxsS4H4Q", "task_type": "webpage_metadata_generation", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "webpage_metadata_generation", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "webpage_markdown", "data": {"window": [[0, "There\u2019s a renewed fascination with homeownership right now, emerging from a hard reality: The age of first-time buyers keeps rising, rents are swallowing household budgets and the starter home has all but disappeared. Policy conversations have rushed toward demand-side fixes such as down-payment assistance, tax credits and even talk of 50-year mortgages, all intended to help buyers stretch further.\n\nBut none of these tools address a core issue: Massachusetts no longer produces many affordable homes for sale.\n\nThe MassINC Policy Center\u2019s 2025 Gateway Cities Housing Monitor report makes the imbalance clear. Roughly 93 percent of state production dollars support rental units, while only 7 percent support for-sale homes. Include federal low-income housing tax credits \u2013 which can only be used for rental \u2013 and the ratio becomes 95 to 5.\n\n**How We Got here**\n\nBefore the Great Recession, roughly a quarter of state housing production dollars flowed to for-sale units, but in reaction to the fore"], [0, "Center for Housing Data - Massachusetts Housing Partnership - MHP\nLaunched in 2023 , Residensity features a user-friendly map platform that allows users to explore and analyze housing unit counts and residential density for any location in Massachusetts ."], [1, "Census Reporter: Making Census Data Easy to Use\nCensus Reporter provides useful facts about every place in America. Compare places using tables and maps , download data, and embed charts on your site!"]], "participants": []}}, "prompt_chain": null, "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["housing policy", "affordable housing", "housing supply", "massachusetts housing", "census data", "interactive map", "interactive maps", "geospatial analysis", "urban planning", "land use", "residential density", "housing units", "demographics", "geographic data", "data visualization", "community profiles", "socioeconomic indicators", "regional comparison", "rental market", "homeownership"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778628197.3771992, "duration_sec": 2.1617846488952637, "validator_hotkey": "5GQyFzvtVMw9X45t6dvUFgR9unFpDCccPPCiAoqJrtPuC8my", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Maybrit Illner. Streit um Rammstein, das w\u00e4re wahrscheinlich das Ende der NATO, warnt Ischina."], [0, "Von Annalena Malta Unter dem Titel Trumps Krieg in Nahost \u2013 Neuer Stresstest f\u00fcr die NATO diskutierte Moderatorin Maybrit Ilner mit dem SPD-Au\u00dfenpolitiker Addis Achmetowitsch, dem Vorsitzenden der M\u00fcnchner Sicherheitskonferenz Wolfgang Ischinger, der \u00d6konomin Veronika Grimm sowie dem Sicherheitsexperten Peter Neumann vom King's College London und Daniel Gerlach, Chefredakteur des Nahostmagazins Zenit."], [0, "US-Pr\u00e4sident Donald Trump verlangt Unterst\u00fctzung im Krieg gegen den Iran, die Bundesregierung lehnt ab, das ist nicht unser Krieg. Genau an diesem Satz entz\u00fcndete sich die Debatte. Ilna fragte, was w\u00e4re, wenn Trump eine \u00e4hnliche Haltung auch gegen\u00fcber der Ukraine einnehme. Alle Entwicklungen zum Iran-Krieg im Live-Ticker. Wolfgang Ischinger kritisierte die Linie der Bundesregierung. In Washington sei ja nur das Nein angekommen, sonst gar nichts anderes. Damit verschenke Deutschland Einfluss."], [0, "Besser w\u00e4re eine europ\u00e4ische Antwort gewesen. Ja, wir k\u00f6nnen das in Betracht ziehen, wir k\u00f6nnen dar\u00fcber nachdenken, aber da h\u00e4tten wir ein paar Gegenforderungen, sagte er. Entscheidend bleibe, f\u00fcr uns in Europa ist das Allerwichtigste und bleibt das Allerwichtigste die Ukraine. Adis Achmetowitsch widersprach deutlich und verteidigte den Kurs des Kanzlers."], [0, "Das Nein zum Irakkrieg von Gerhard Schr\u00f6der 2003 war genau richtig, sagte er, und ich bin dem Bundeskanzler sehr dankbar f\u00fcr diese klaren Worte gestern im Deutschen Bundestag. Dann wurde er noch deutlicher, dieser Krieg ist nicht unser. Dieser Krieg ist falsch. Dieser Krieg ist ein schwerer Fehler. Und weiter, dieser Krieg ist auch v\u00f6lkerrechtswidrig."], [0, "Die Moderatorin hakte ein und fragte, ob sich Deutschland denn dann strafbar mache, wenn es den Krieg indirekt unterst\u00fctze mit dem US-St\u00fctzpunkt in Rammstein bei Kaiserslautern. Ahmetowitsch verwies auf die Pr\u00fcfung dieser Frage durch das Ausw\u00e4rtige Amt. Je nach Ausgang der Au\u00dfenamtspr\u00fcfung k\u00f6nnten Gerichte anordnen, dass Rammstein f\u00fcr diesen Krieg im Iran nicht genutzt werden kann."], [0, "Sei es v\u00f6lkerrechtswidrig, werde das eine Diskussion im Deutschen Bundestag sein und auch eine Rechtsfrage. Bei diesen \u00c4u\u00dferungen schmunzelte Ischinger. Die Pr\u00fcfung durch das Ausw\u00e4rtige Amt werde positiv ausfallen, betonte er. Jede andere Entscheidung w\u00e4re wahrscheinlich mehr oder weniger das Ende der NATO."], [0, "Von der US-Luftwaffenbasis in Deutschland w\u00fcrden keine m\u00f6rderischen Angriffe auf den Iran geflogen, sondern vor allem milit\u00e4rische G\u00fcter transportiert. Das Ausw\u00e4rtige Amt werde sich schwer tun, festzustellen, dass die Rammsteinfl\u00fcge eine systematische V\u00f6lkerrechtsverletzung seien, Achmetovic nickte. Man kann nicht sagen, dass es nicht unser Krieg ist."], [0, "Veronika Grimm widersprach der Regierungsformel Das ist nicht unser Krieg aus \u00f6konomischer Sicht. Ich glaube, man kann nicht sagen, dass es nicht unser Krieg ist, sagte sie, weil, die Auswirkungen dieser Eskalation werden wir ganz deutlich zu sp\u00fcren bekommen. Sie verwies auf drohende Preissteigerungen und sagte, der Konflikt k\u00f6nnte 1 bis 1,3 Prozentpunkte obendrauf geben bei der Inflationsrate."], [0, "Zugleich nannte sie als m\u00f6gliches positives Szenario, dass ein geschw\u00e4chter Iran aus dem Block mit China und Russland herausgel\u00f6st werden k\u00f6nnte. Eine gro\u00dfe Chance f\u00fcr Europa. Daniel Gerlach ordnete die Lage aus regionaler Perspektive ein. Die Amerikaner haben sich verkalkuliert, sagte er, sie seien sehr optimistisch daran gegangen."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["News & Politics"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["nato", "iran war", "middle east", "trump", "germany politics", "ukraine", "european response", "rammstein base", "international law", "foreign ministry", "military support", "inflation", "security conference", "economics", "china", "russia", "diplomacy", "energy prices"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
