{"timestamp": 1778629622.776637, "duration_sec": 2.8326003551483154, "validator_hotkey": "5FZe9Mpo5dLXfhGZ4VjRnw6dmz9LVPp6nzqPyDfaS9BLKs33", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Good morning, it's February 18th and this is your daily brief in AI. Here's everything you need to know."], [1, "AI takes center stage at BioAsia 2026 in Hyderabad as Asia's leading life sciences and health tech forum opens its 23rd edition with a sharp focus on AI, automation, and data science to accelerate healthcare innovation. More than 175 exhibitors spanning pharmaceuticals, biotechnology, medtech, digital health, and advanced manufacturing showcase a broad tech-bio ecosystem. The event brings researchers, entrepreneurs, investors, and policymakers together to push the tech-bio revolution and address global health challenges. Telangana highlights its strong policies, skilled workforce, and premier educational institutions as key drivers of growth in life sciences. The opening ceremony, led by the State Chief Minister, included the Genome Valley Excellence Award for Cancer Gene Therapy to Professor Bruce L. Levine. Inauguration and awards underscore Telangana's leadership in life sciences and recognize Levine's work in cancer gene therapy. Telangana also unveiled initiatives such as the Young India Skills University and the Telangana School of Life Sciences to build talent in mRNA technology, gene therapy, and AI. Recent moves cited include the Telangana Next Gen Life Sciences Policy, Genome Valley expansion, the launch of OneBio and multiple global capability centers in Hyderabad, The event emphasized ongoing collaborations among research institutions, corporates, startups, MSMEs, and government to create a trusted, future-ready life sciences ecosystem in Telangana. Telangana Rising 2047 envisions making the state a $1 trillion economy by year 2034 and $3 trillion by year 2047 through cross-sector collaboration across research labs, industry, startups, MSMEs, and government. The Telangana Life Sciences Policy 2026-30 promotes cross-border collaboration, international capital, and translation of breakthroughs into healthcare solutions to position Telangana as a global life sciences hub. Plans include shifting from supply-led manufacturing to solution-driven leadership by building talent in mRNA, gene editing, and AI-driven drug discovery, while boosting Hyderabad's role in medical tourism."], [2, "Unilever is partnering with a major cloud provider to run an AI-first digital overhaul, migrating its data and cloud platform to Google Cloud to speed demand generation and deliver actionable insights. The initiative centers on flagship brands Dove, Vaseline, and Hellmann's as consumer journeys become more AI-driven and conversational, aiming to redefine how consumer packaged goods are discovered and shopped. Leaders describe it as a milestone in modernizing legacy systems and boosting agility and consumer engagement in the CPG sector. Market reaction showed UL trading near its 52-week high, with a pre-market around $74.65 and approaching the annual high of $74.97. Unilever reported strong fiscal 2025 results, with total sales up 3.8% to \u20ac50.5 billion across Beauty Wellbeing, personal care, and home care. The collaboration is framed as part of a broader shift toward agentic consumer journeys where AI surfaces influence product discovery and selection. It aims to redefine how brands are found and purchased, aligning with increasingly conversational journeys guided by intelligent digital agents. There is mention of repurposing a former Unilever soap factory in Wales into a modular data center site, signaling broader data infrastructure development alongside the cloud migration. The initiative seeks more personalized consumer engagement and more efficient marketing investments, signaling a move toward AI-driven experiences in the CPG space. Unilever's longstanding relationship with Accenture, renewed in 2024 to scale GenAI, complements Horizon 3 Labs' efforts in Toronto that reportedly runs hundreds of AI applications. The partnership signals a broader industry shift toward AI-enabled transformation in marketing, data infrastructure, and automated business processes within consumer goods, with overhauls of marketing processes to establish new measurement standards, increase conversion rates, and accelerate AI adoption across global."], [3, "Operations."], [4, "The ASM AI Fest 2026 runs through February 28th, showcasing an AI-first mindset across teaching, research, learning methods, and administration to prepare graduates and staff for pervasive AI adoption. The festival features world-class AI workshops that move beyond awareness to practical AI applications, aiming for AI to amplify human capability rather than substitute it. It concludes with a closing ceremony on February 28th, reinforcing ASM's leadership in AI-integrated education across MBA, PGDM, MCA, engineering, undergraduate studies, and school and junior college. A press release includes a photo and logo link and carries an advertorial disclaimer noting the content was provided by PR Newswire and not authored by Business Standard journalists. The initiative is described as one of the region's largest AI-driven academic efforts and positions ASM as a pioneer in AI-integrated education aligned with national AI objectives. As part of the sustained transformation, ASM will form institute-wide AI task forces, establish the ASM AI Center of Excellence, deploy the Navdrishti app for automated student lifecycle management, and introduce AI into PGDM dual specialization programs. The long-term roadmap includes institute-wise AI task forces, a center of excellence for training and research, and the Navdrishti app with AI-enabled placements and broader expansion into academics and finances. Institutional AI roadmap highlights creating task forces, a COE for training and research, and Navdrishti for automated student lifecycle management, with initial AI-enabled placements and later expansion. AI integration spans the entire ASM academic spectrum, from MBA, PGEM, MCA, and engineering to undergraduate and school junior college, preparing learners for a future with pervasive AI adoption. A PGDM dual specialization program with AI integration was launched, signaling program-level AI incorporation across curricula. Program implications include AI-driven analytics for MBA PGDM, ML tools for MCA engineering, AI-influenced entrepreneurship, and data-driven decisions for undergraduates, and foundational AI literacy for younger students. The initiative aligns with India's India AI Mission and Digital India, aiming to position India as a global hub for AI talent and to embed AI across education and administration."], [3, "Ant Group expands its open-source AI family with two trillion-parameter models, Ling-2.5-1T and Ring-2.5-1T, released under open licenses on Hugging Face and ModelScope. The move continues Ling's ecosystem expansion following Ling 2.0 unveiled in late 2025 and positions Ant Group as a key proponent of open AI distribution for researchers and developers. Ling-2.5-1T is described as a flagship general language model focused on efficient reasoning and agent interaction, capable of handling context lengths up to 1 million tokens while using about 5,890 tokens to reach frontier-like results. Ring-2.5-1T is a reasoning-optimized model with a hybrid linear architecture, delivering strong mathematical performance on IMO 2025 and CMO 2025 benchmarks. Both models are part of a coordinated Ling, Ring, and Ming strategy aimed at enterprise AI deployments that combine language understanding, reasoning, and multimodal capabilities for financial services. The open-release approach seeks to accelerate ecosystem adoption by enabling external developers to build domain-specific finance applications, potentially reducing costs and enabling larger-scale deployments. Ant Group frames these releases within a broader fintech trend of integrating large language models and reasoning systems into tasks such as compliance, customer interactions, and risk assessment. Open Access Positions: Ant Group among global contributors to open large-scale AI and supports adapting models for financial domain tasks by external developers. The Ling-2.5-1T release emphasizes efficient reasoning and agent interaction, while Ring-2.5-1T targets higher-order mathematical reasoning and benchmark performance. Overall, the announcements underscore a move toward open, collaborative AI infrastructure designed to support enterprise-grade finance use."], [0, "Cases. Tech is expanding its AI-driven frontline performance ecosystem, anchored by Realskill and Perform, to serve more than 100 enterprise clients and over 25,000 frontline agents worldwide. The goal is to improve associate proficiency and performance, including sales, across global contact centers as part of enterprise adoption. Julie Stone notes that AI alone doesn't drive performance. Translating AI insights into everyday behaviors through realistic practice and timely coaching is essential. The approach links immersive AI-powered practice, performance intelligence, and closed-loop coaching to convert AI insights into daily tasks and repeatable results, eliminating silos between learning, coaching, and execution. The ecosystem centers on RealSkill and Perform to create a continuous skills and behavior framework from onboarding through optimization, with a real-time view of frontline effectiveness. Client examples show tangible outcomes, including a 10% sales increase for an insurance firm and 17-23% NPS boosts for healthcare and telecom clients through data-informed coaching. It positio